## About

I am a final-year Computer Engineering student at İzmir Bakırçay University. I build software across game development, full-stack applications, developer tools, and applied AI.

My interests lie in the systems behind the interface: gameplay architecture, data integrity, local-first design, deterministic processing, model evaluation, and reliable release workflows. I enjoy taking an idea from experiment to a usable product and understanding the trade-offs along the way.

[ArtifactHub](https://artifacthub.baglare.com.tr/) is my technical portfolio: architecture, design decisions, implemented scope, evidence, and known limitations for each project.

## Project index

Projects are grouped by engineering domain rather than ranked. Status labels distinguish deployed products, released tools, active development, and experimental work.

### Game development

| Project | Status | Engineering focus |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [Fly Butterfly](https://artifacthub.baglare.com.tr/artifacts/butterfly-effect/) | Graduation project · in development | Two-player, dual-era Unity game with networked state, deterministic causality, and player-specific knowledge. Unity, C#, Netcode for GameObjects. |
| [PulseForge](https://github.com/Baglare/PulseForge) · [Case study](https://artifacthub.baglare.com.tr/artifacts/pulseforge/) | Prototype | Turns user-selected audio into rhythm-combat encounters through onset and beat analysis, seeded planning, and DSP-based timing. Unity, C#, FFmpeg. |
| [TempoBlade](https://github.com/Baglare/TempoBlade) · [Case study](https://artifacthub.baglare.com.tr/artifacts/tempoblade/) | Prototype | Tempo-driven action roguelite with parry/deflect, data-driven weapons, encounters, and progression. Unity, C#, ScriptableObjects. |

